#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:5
msgid ""
"Transforms CSS declaration values and at-rule parameters into a tree of "
"nodes, and provides a simple traversal API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:7
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:17
msgid ""
"For example, parsing the value `rgba(233, 45, 66, .5)` will return the "
"following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:41
msgid ""
"If you wanted to convert each `rgba()` value in `sourceCSS` to a hex "
"value, you could do so like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:73
msgid "Nodes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:75
msgid "Each node is an object with these common properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:77
msgid ""
"**type**: The type of node (`word`, `string`, `div`, `space`, `comment`, "
"or `function`). Each type is documented below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:79
msgid ""
"**value**: Each node has a `value` property; but what exactly `value` "
"means is specific to the node type. Details are documented for each type "
"below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:81
msgid ""
"**sourceIndex**: The starting index of the node within the original "
"source string. For example, given the source string `10px 20px`, the "
"`word` node whose value is `20px` will have a `sourceIndex` of `5`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:85
msgid "word"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:87
msgid ""
"The catch-all node type that includes keywords (e.g. `no-repeat`), "
"quantities (e.g. `20px`, `75%`, `1.5`), and hex colors (e.g. `#e6e6e6`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:90
#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:98
#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:112
#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:122
#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:130
msgid "Node-specific properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:92
msgid "**value**: The \"word\" itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:94
msgid "string"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:96
msgid "A quoted string value, e.g. `\"something\"` in `content: \"something\";`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:100
msgid "**value**: The text content of the string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:101
msgid "**quote**: The quotation mark surrounding the string, either `\"` or `'`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:102
msgid ""
"**unclosed**: `true` if the string was not closed properly. e.g. "
"`\"unclosed string  `."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:104
msgid "div"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:106
msgid "A divider, for example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:108
msgid "`,` in `animation-duration: 1s, 2s, 3s`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:109
msgid "`/` in `border-radius: 10px / 23px`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:110
msgid "`:` in `(min-width: 700px)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:114
msgid ""
"**value**: The divider character. Either `,`, `/`, or `:` (see examples "
"above)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:115
msgid "**before**: Whitespace before the divider."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:116
msgid "**after**: Whitespace after the divider."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:118
msgid "space"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:120
msgid ""
"Whitespace used as a separator, e.g. ` ` occurring twice in `border: 1px "
"solid black;`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:124
msgid "**value**: The whitespace itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:126
msgid "comment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:128
msgid "A CSS comment starts with `/*` and ends with `*/`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:132
msgid "**value**: The comment value without `/*` and `*/`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:133
msgid ""
"**unclosed**: `true` if the comment was not closed properly. e.g. `/* "
"comment without an end  `."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:135
msgid "function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:137
msgid "A CSS function, e.g. `rgb(0,0,0)` or `url(foo.bar)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:139
msgid "Function nodes have nodes nested within them: the function arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:141
msgid "Additional properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:143
msgid "**value**: The name of the function, e.g. `rgb` in `rgb(0,0,0)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:144
msgid ""
"**before**: Whitespace after the opening parenthesis and before the first"
" argument, e.g. `  ` in `rgb(  0,0,0)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:146
msgid ""
"**after**: Whitespace before the closing parenthesis and after the last "
"argument, e.g. `  ` in `rgb(0,0,0  )`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:148
msgid "**nodes**: More nodes representing the arguments to the function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:149
msgid ""
"**unclosed**: `true` if the parentheses was not closed properly. e.g. `( "
"unclosed-function  `."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:151
msgid ""
"Media features surrounded by parentheses are considered functions with an"
" empty value. For example, `(min-width: 700px)` parses to these nodes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:167
msgid ""
"`url()` functions can be parsed a little bit differently depending on "
"whether the first character in the argument is a quotation mark."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:170
msgid "`url( /gfx/img/bg.jpg )` parses to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:178
msgid "`url( \"/gfx/img/bg.jpg\" )`, on the other hand, parses to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:186
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:192
msgid "valueParser.unit(quantity)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:194
msgid ""
"Parses `quantity`, distinguishing the number from the unit. Returns an "
"object like the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:204
msgid "If the `quantity` argument cannot be parsed as a number, returns `false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:206
msgid ""
"*This function does not parse complete values*: you cannot pass it `1px "
"solid black` and expect `px` as the unit. Instead, you should pass it "
"single quantities only. Parse `1px solid black`, then pass it the "
"stringified `1px` node (a `word` node) to parse the number and unit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:210
msgid "valueParser.stringify(nodes[, custom])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:212
msgid "Stringifies a node or array of nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:214
msgid ""
"The `custom` function is called for each `node`; return a string to "
"override the default behaviour."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:216
msgid "valueParser.walk(nodes, callback[, bubble])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:218
msgid ""
"Walks each provided node, recursively walking all descendent nodes within"
" functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:220
msgid ""
"Returning `false` in the `callback` will prevent traversal of descendent "
"nodes (within functions). You can use this feature to for shallow "
"iteration, walking over only the *immediate* children. *Note: This only "
"applies if `bubble` is `false` (which is the default).*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:224
msgid ""
"By default, the tree is walked from the outermost node inwards. To "
"reverse the direction, pass `true` for the `bubble` argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:227
msgid ""
"The `callback` is invoked with three arguments: `callback(node, index, "
"nodes)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:229
msgid "`node`: The current node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:230
msgid "`index`: The index of the current node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:231
msgid "`nodes`: The complete nodes array passed to `walk()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:233
msgid "Returns the `valueParser` instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:235
msgid "var parsed = valueParser(value)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:237
msgid "Returns the parsed node tree."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:239
msgid "parsed.nodes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:241
msgid "The array of nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:243
msgid "parsed.toString()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:245
msgid "Stringifies the node tree."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:247
msgid "parsed.walk(callback[, bubble])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/postcss-value-parser_README.md:249
msgid ""
"Walks each node inside `parsed.nodes`. See the documentation for "
"`valueParser.walk()` above."
msgstr ""

